# tools/text_marquee_witness.rish -- the open video codecs prove themselves on REAL panning motion (Season G).
#
# Season G's capstone (tools/text_reel_witness.rish) proved both open video codecs on a typewriter reveal -- the EASY
# case for inter-frame storage, where each frame changes only the newly shown glyph so the delta always wins. This
# witness proves the HARD case: image/text_marquee.rye renders a wide caption strip ONCE with the finished
# font-and-paint family, then crops one frame per step to scroll the caption left through a fixed window -- REAL
# panning motion, where the whole inked band slides sideways every frame and many pixels change at once.
#
# The crux is the ADAPTIVE codec earning its keep on content that does not favour it: gfd1 chooses per frame the
# smaller of a pixel delta or a whole keyframe, so heavy panning is exactly where it must fall back to keyframes rather
# than store a delta larger than a frame. This witness proves the round-trip stays byte-for-byte through BOTH codecs
# under that motion, and REPORTS the delta/keyframe mix rather than claiming a compression win (on real panning it may
# not win -- the honest proof is correctness under motion). No network, no key, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/text_marquee_witness.rish

say "text-marquee: Language EN -- Season G's hard case; the open video codecs proven on REAL panning motion where the whole band slides each frame, real frames that reconstruct within named bounds rather than playing garbage."
say "text-marquee: Style Radiant -- a caption rendered once onto a wide strip and cropped frame by frame into a marquee, fed through both open codecs; decode(encode(reel)) recovers every frame byte for byte under motion the delta cannot always win."
say "text-marquee: Lens TAME -- u32 in-memory counts, u8 pixel bytes; every buffer names a maximum (marquee_max_frames, the codecs' encoded_bound, the QOI ceilings beneath); each function states its invariants positively; the delta/keyframe mix a reported measurement, never a false compression claim; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/text_marquee"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/text_marquee.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "text-marquee: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "text-marquee: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "text-marquee: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-text-marquee" else "text-marquee: selftest did not print the GREEN panning line"

assert selftest.out contains "round-trip byte-identical through BOTH codecs under REAL panning" else "text-marquee: the panning reel did not round-trip through both codecs"

assert selftest.out contains "adaptive mix" else "text-marquee: the adaptive delta/keyframe mix was not reported"

say "text-marquee: GREEN -- the open video codecs whole under motion; a real panning reel round-trips byte-identical through both open codecs, the adaptive delta/keyframe mix reported honestly, the two formats distinct by name."
